#: buildVars.py:19
#| msgid ""
#| "FreeRadio is an internet radio, podcast, and audio-book add-on for NVDA "
#| "that provides seamless access to thousands of internet radio stations via "
#| "the Radio Browser open directory, RSS/Atom podcast feeds, and the libriVox "
#| "+ GETEM digital library for the visually impaired. It features a fully "
#| "accessible station browser with search, country filter, favourites "
#| "management, and per-station, per-podcast, and per-audio-book audio "
#| "profiles. Podcast episodes and audio book chapters resume automatically "
#| "from where you left off, with adjustable pitch-preserving playback speed. "
#| "Playback is handled by BASS, with support for volume control, audio "
#| "effects, output device selection, and simultaneous audio mirroring to a "
#| "second device. Additional features include instant and scheduled "
#| "recording, time-shift rewind of live radio, sleep and alarm timers, "
#| "automatic ICY metadata announcements, Shazam-based music recognition, and "
#| "a liked-songs log with lyrics lookup. All controls and shortcuts are "
#| "designed for NVDA accessibility."
msgid ""
"FreeRadio is an internet radio, podcast, audio-book, and local music add-on "
"for NVDA that provides seamless access to thousands of internet radio "
"stations via the Radio Browser open directory, RSS/Atom podcast feeds, the "
"libriVox + GETEM digital library for the visually impaired, and your own "
"local audio files and folders through its built-in jukebox. It features a "
"fully accessible station browser with search, country filter, favourites "
"management, and per-station, per-podcast, per-audio-book, and per-jukebox-"
"track audio profiles. Podcast episodes, audio book chapters, and jukebox "
"tracks resume automatically from where you left off - jukebox folders even "
"pick up on the last track you were playing - with adjustable pitch-preserving "
"playback speed and independent pitch-shift (semitone transpose). Playback is "
"handled by BASS, with support for volume control, audio effects, output "
"device selection, and simultaneous audio mirroring to a second device. "
"Additional features include instant and scheduled recording, time-shift "
"rewind of live radio, sleep and alarm timers, automatic ICY metadata "
"announcements, Shazam-based music recognition, and a liked-songs log with "
"lyrics lookup. All controls and shortcuts are designed for NVDA accessibility."
msgstr ""

#: buildVars.py:26
msgid ""
"\n"
"## New features:\n"
"- Local Jukebox tab: search audio files stored on any attached drive by "
"filename, or build a persistent personal library of files and folders. "
"Jukebox tracks get the same treatment as podcasts and audio books: automatic "
"resume, tiered rewind/fast-forward, playback speed, pitch transpose, and per-"
"item audio profiles. Open the Jukebox tab from anywhere with Ctrl+Win+U, or "
"from the Station Browser with Alt+8.\n"
"- Transpose (pitch shift): shift the pitch of podcasts, audio books, and "
"jukebox tracks up or down without changing their speed, using Shift+Win+K "
"(raise) and Shift+Win+J (lower). Each step is one eighth of a whole tone "
"(0.25 semitones); the range is -12.00 to +12.00 semitones. Requires "
"bass_fx.dll.\n"
"- Jukebox tab keyboard shortcuts: F3 / F4 move between tracks within the "
"selected jukebox item; Shift+F3 / Shift+F4 move between jukebox entries; "
"Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right do the same as F3 / F4 while the tracks or entries "
"list is focused. Space previews a disk-search result or pauses the current "
"playback; Enter adds a disk-search result to the jukebox or plays the focused "
"item directly.\n"
"\n"
"Improvements:\n"
"- Playback speed shortcuts (Ctrl+Win+Shift+K / Ctrl+Win+Shift+J) now also "
"apply to jukebox tracks, not just podcasts and audio books.\n"
"- Ctrl+Win+V (Add to Favourites / Download Media) now tells the user "
"explicitly that the shortcut only applies to stations, podcasts, and audio "
"books when a jukebox track is currently playing, instead of silently treating "
"the jukebox track as a station.\n"
"- The Station Browser now contains eight tabs instead of seven; tab "
"navigation shortcuts run from Alt+1 through Alt+8.\n"
"- Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab tab cycling now includes the Jukebox tab.\n"
"- Ctrl+Win+I (What's playing) now also announces jukebox track names.\n"
"- Ctrl+Win+J and Ctrl+Win+K (tiered seek) now also work on jukebox tracks.\n"
"- Ctrl+Win+T (Toggle time-shift buffer) now clarifies that it has no effect "
"on podcast, audio book, or jukebox playback.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"## Nuevas funciones: - Pestaña Jukebox local: busca archivos de audio "
"almacenados en cualquier unidad conectada por nombre de archivo, o crea una "
"biblioteca personal persistente de archivos y carpetas. Las pistas de Jukebox "
"reciben el mismo tratamiento que los podcasts y audiolibros: reanudación "
"automática, rebobinado/avance rápido por niveles, velocidad de reproducción, "
"transposición de tono y perfiles de audio por elemento. Abre la pestaña "
"Jukebox desde cualquier lugar con Ctrl+Win+U, o desde el Explorador de "
"estaciones con Alt+8.\n"
"- Transposición (cambio de tono): cambia el tono de podcasts, audiolibros y "
"pistas del Jukebox hacia arriba o hacia abajo sin cambiar su velocidad, "
"usando Shift+Win+K (subir) y Shift+Win+J (bajar). Cada paso es un octavo de "
"tono completo (0,25 semitonos); el rango es de -12,00 a +12,00 semitonos. "
"Requiere el bass_fx.dll.\n"
"- Atajos de teclado para la pestaña Jukebox: F3 / F4 se mueven entre las "
"pistas dentro del elemento seleccionado del Jukebox; Shift+F3 / Shift+F4 "
"permite navegar entre las entradas de la lista de reproducción; "
"Ctrl+Izquierda / Ctrl+Derecha realiza la misma función que F3 / F4 mientras "
"la lista de pistas o entradas está seleccionada. La barra espaciadora muestra "
"una vista previa del resultado de la búsqueda en disco o pausa la "
"reproducción actual; Intro añade un resultado de la búsqueda en disco a la "
"lista de reproducción o reproduce directamente el elemento seleccionado.\n"
"\n"
"Mejoras:\n"
"- Los atajos de velocidad de reproducción (Ctrl+Win+Shift+K / "
"Ctrl+Win+Shift+J) ahora también se aplican a las pistas de la lista de "
"reproducción, no solo a podcasts y audiolibros.\n"
"- Ctrl+Win+V (Añadir a Favoritos / Descargar el Medio) ahora indica "
"explícitamente al usuario que el atajo solo se aplica a emisoras, podcasts y "
"audiolibros cuando se está reproduciendo una pista de la lista de "
"reproducción.En lugar de tratar silenciosamente la pista del jukebox como una "
"emisora.\n"
"- El navegador de emisoras ahora contiene ocho pestañas en lugar de siete; "
"los atajos de navegación entre pestañas van desde Alt+1 hasta Alt+8.\n"
"- El cambio de pestañas con Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab ahora incluye la "
"pestaña del Jukebox .\n"
"- Ctrl+Win+I (¿Qué se está reproduciendo?) ahora también anuncia los nombres "
"de las pistas del jukebox.\n"
"- Ctrl+Win+J y Ctrl+Win+K (búsqueda por niveles) ahora también funcionan en "
"las pistas del jukebox.\n"
"- Ctrl+Win+T (Alternar búfer de desplazamiento temporal) ahora aclara que no "
"tiene efecto en la reproducción de podcasts, audiolibros o la del jukebox.\n"

